## Ingredients

### Taco Seasoning

_Or use store bought seasoning_

- [ ] 1 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 15-ounce can [fire roasted tomatoes]{ ing="fire-roasted-tomatoes" }

### Tacos

- [ ] [Instant Pot]{ ing="instant-pot" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 2.5 lbs [boneless skinless chicken]{ ing="boneless-skinless-chicken" } (thighs, breast, etc.)
- [ ] 1/2 cup [Salsa]{ ing="salsa" }
- [ ] [Taco Seasoning]{ ing="taco-seasoning" } (above)

### Serving

- [ ] Corn or [flour taco-size tortillas]{ ing="flour-taco-size-tortillas" }
- [ ] [Shredded cheese]{ ing="shredded-cheese" } (Cheddar, Monterrey Jack, or Mix)
- [ ] [Shredded lettuce]{ ing="shredded-lettuce" }, cabbage, or baby spinach
- [ ] [Tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, diced
- [ ] [Onions]{ ing="onions" }, diced
- [ ] [Lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }
- [ ] [Cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }
- [ ] [Salsa]{ ing="salsa" }
- [ ] [Hot Sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" }
- [ ] [Sour cream]{ ing="sour-cream" }
- [ ] [Avocado slices]{ ing="avocado-slices" } or Guacamole
- [ ] Sliced pickled or fresh [jalapeños]{ ing="jalapenos" }
- [ ] [Thinly sliced radishes]{ ing="thinly-sliced-radishes" }

## Recipe

1. Place 1/2 cup of [water]{ ing="water" } in an [instant pot]{ ing="instant-pot" }. Add the [chicken]{ ing="boneless-skinless-chicken" } and coat with [taco seasoning]{ ing="taco-seasoning" } (store bought or DIY seasoning) and top with the 1/2 cup of [salsa]{ ing="salsa" }

   1. Cook for 20-30 min (depending on size) at low heat and high pressure. Quick release and shred (pull apart) with 2 forks
1. Serve on tacos, in a Quesadillas, or in a sandwich

### (Optional) Creamy Avocado Sauce Recipe

- [ ] Lime, juiced (2 Tbsp)
- [ ] Avocado, pitted and peeled
- [ ] 1/3 cup sour cream or plain Greek yogurt
- [ ] 1/2 tsp kosher salt

1. Place the lime juice in a mini food processor.
Add the avocado, sour cream, and salt.
Process until smooth.
Thin out with more lime juice if desired
